if(b=t.closest('[data-j]')){const j=J[+b.dataset.j],p=byId(j[3]);$('#md').innerHTML=`<div class="in"><button class="lab" data-x style="margin-bottom:30px">← Close</button><span class="lab" style="color:var(--mut)">${j[0]} · ${j[4]}</span><h2>${j[1]}</h2><div class="im">${PI(p,p.colors[0],4)}</div><p style="font-size:19px;font-family:var(--serif)">${j[2]}</p><p>We begin each season with a question rather than a mood board. What can be taken away? What remains when a garment is stripped to its proportion, its cloth and its cut?</p><p>The answer is rarely dramatic. It lives in a collar that sits a fraction lower, a hem that falls with the weight of the wool, a sleeve that moves before you do. This is the work: slow, exacting, and invisible when it succeeds.</p><p>Wear it often. Let it soften. The best pieces never announce themselves; they simply become yours.</p></div>`;hydrate($('#md'));$('#md').classList.add('on');document.body.style.overflow='hidden';$('#md').scrollTop=0;return}
